Z||000002||Mach10||08-30-2001||04:51 PM||||Sushi is japanese... But still funny as hell. I had a book of "101 of the stupidest things ever done"<P>My favorite was a Japanese foundry that developed a carbon steel rod of unusual strength. Their marketing Genius called it "Super High Toughness" rods. Of course, acronyms are the "in" thing, so it became "SHT"<BR>The resulting Ad campains read:<BR>"&lt;foundry name escapes me&gt; brings SHT to America!"<BR>"Our SHT is stronger!"<P>Love it, don't you?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
